/// An integer literal keeps its value.
///
/// A literal too large for Integer is silently truncated to 32 bits by both
/// processors: 10000000000 reads as 1410065408, with no diagnostic and exit 0.
///
/// ⚠️ This is not the same thing as Integer arithmetic wrapping, which is
/// specified.  2147483647 + 1 wrapping is a computation on values the author
/// wrote; here the LITERAL ITSELF is altered before the program starts, which
/// no arithmetic rule covers.  A constant is the one place a processor always
/// has enough information to refuse.
///
/// The spec gives a literal the narrowest of Integer and Long that holds it, so
/// this one is a Long.  Fixing it without Long is still worth doing, and means
/// refusing the literal rather than promoting it.
///
/// Fails with: Assertion 'left = right' failed.  Expected '10000000000' but got '1410065408'.
///
test 'An integer literal keeps its value';
begin
    var Big := 10000000000;

    AssertEqual ('10000000000', Str (Big));
    AssertTrue  (Big > 2147483647);
end
